and are licensed under the MIT License, the same licence this repository uses.

This file exists because that attribution belongs beside the licence rather
than inside it. GitHub's licence classifier matches the body of LICENSE against
known texts, and any prose between the copyright line and the permission grant
makes it report `NOASSERTION` -- "Other" -- on a repository that is plainly
MIT. The attribution was there first and had exactly that effect.
